<title>CHILE: Chile forex reserves fall to $15.2 billion.</title>
<headline>Chile forex reserves fall to $15.2 billion.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's international reserves dropped $68 million in the first two weeks of the month to total $15.2 billion on October 15, said the central bank in its fortnightly report.</p>
<p>The fall was the result of a $69 million deficit in the balance of payments account and a $1 million increase in the value of the reserves as the result of exchange rate fluctuations, it said.</p>
<p>--Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212</p>
